<% content_for :title, "Import / Export · Railpress" %>
<p class="eyebrow">Tools</p><h1>Import / Export</h1>
<p>Move approved website content using Railpress site archive v3; older v2 archives remain readable. Older destinations must be upgraded before reading v3. Archives are plaintext content packages, not backups or executable themes. Existing accounts, credentials and operator settings stay on this installation.</p>
<section class="admin-card"><h2>Export a site archive</h2>
<%= form_with url: admin_site_exports_path, data: {turbo: false} do %>
<label for="export-mode">Export scope</label><select name="mode" id="export-mode"><option value="public">Public snapshots only (default)</option><option value="owner_private">Explicitly selected private working copies</option></select>
<p>Public scope excludes every private draft and revision. Private scope requires selecting the exact content below. A published item's private working edit is included only in private scope.</p>
<details><summary>Select private content</summary><% @contents.each do |content| %><label><%= check_box_tag "content_ids[]", content.id, false %> <%= content.type %>: <%= content.title %> · <%= content.status %></label><% end %></details>
<label><%= check_box_tag :history, "1", false %> Approve full selected revision history (private scope only)</label>
<label><%= check_box_tag :menus, "1", true %> Include menus and independent draft/live location assignments</label>
<label><%= check_box_tag :appearance, "1", false %> Include trusted theme reference and customization overlay</label>
<details><summary>Approved portable author labels (optional, private scope only)</summary><p>Blank labels omit login identities. These labels do not create destination accounts.</p><% @authors.each do |author| %><label for="author-label-<%= author.id %>"><%= author.username %>: approved export label</label><%= text_field_tag "author_labels[#{author.id}]", "", id: "author-label-#{author.id}", maxlength: 120 %><% end %></details>
<details><summary>Media rights and attribution</summary><p>Every referenced media object requires explicit current clearance. Unselected objects are not exported.</p><% @assets.each do |asset| %><fieldset><legend><%= asset.title %></legend><label><%= check_box_tag "media_rights[#{asset.id}][confirmed]", "1", false %> I confirm current export rights for this object and its variants</label><label for="license-<%= asset.id %>">License or permission</label><%= text_field_tag "media_rights[#{asset.id}][license]", asset.license_notes, id: "license-#{asset.id}", maxlength: 1000 %><label for="attribution-<%= asset.id %>">Approved attribution</label><%= text_field_tag "media_rights[#{asset.id}][attribution]", asset.attribution, id: "attribution-#{asset.id}", maxlength: 1000 %></fieldset><% end %></details>
<p>Limits: 500 content records, 2,000 revisions, 64 media objects and 128 MiB. Protect downloaded private archives using access controls and encrypted storage/transport.</p><button>Request archive export</button>
<% end %></section>
<section class="admin-card"><h2>Inspect an archive</h2><p>Upload an uncompressed .railpress archive. Validation and dry run run in the native worker. No destination content is changed until you review and approve private staging.</p>
<%= form_with url: admin_imports_path, multipart: true, data: {turbo: false} do %><%= hidden_field_tag :idempotency_key, @idempotency_key %><label for="import-archive">Railpress archive (up to 128 MiB)</label><%= file_field_tag :archive, id: "import-archive", required: true, accept: ".railpress" %><button>Upload for inspection</button><% end %></section>
<section class="admin-card"><h2>Recent imports</h2><% if @batches.empty? %><p>No imports yet. Start with an archive inspection; it does not publish content.</p><% else %><ul class="admin-list"><% @batches.each do |batch| %><li><%= link_to "Import #{batch.public_id.first(8)}", admin_import_path(batch.public_id) %><span><%= batch.state %> · <%= batch.progress %>/<%= batch.total %></span></li><% end %></ul><% end %></section>
<section class="admin-card"><h2>Recent exports</h2><ul class="admin-list"><% @exports.each do |record| %><li><%= link_to "Export #{record.public_id.first(8)}", admin_site_export_path(record.public_id) %> <%= record.scope["mode"] %> · <%= record.state %></li><% end %></ul></section>
<details><summary>Earlier manifest compatibility</summary><p>The JSON-only content manifest v1 contains references and revision hashes. It is not a complete archive and cannot be imported as v2.</p><%= link_to "Export content manifest v1", new_admin_export_path %></details>
